Subject: [RFC PATCH 0/8] DAMON mTHP collapse/split with SPE hot/cold detection

This series adds mTHP collapse and split actions to DAMON, with
sub-THP access heatmap feedback via ARM SPE for intelligent split
decisions.

Overview
========

DAMON currently only monitors access patterns.  This series extends it
to actively manage transparent hugepages: collapsing smaller mTHPs into
PMD-sized THPs when beneficial, and splitting PMD THPs into smaller
mTHPs when only a fraction of the THP is hot.

The split decision uses ARM SPE (Statistical Profiling Extension,
ARMv8.2+) to track per-subpage access counts within each THP, building
a heatmap that identifies which subpages are cold and can be split away.

Architecture
============

Collapse (patches 1-3,7):
  DAMON scheme with DAMOS_COLLAPSE action + target_order
  -> damos_va_collapse()
  -> damon_collapse_folio_range()  [khugepaged wrapper]
  -> collapse_huge_page()          [existing khugepaged logic]

Split (patches 4-8):
  DAMON scheme with DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action + target_order
  -> damos_va_mthp_split()
  -> damon_spe_hot_fraction()       [sub-THP heatmap query]
  -> split_folio_to_order()         [if cold enough]

SPE feedback (patches 6,8):
  ARM SPE samples -> {phys_addr, access_type}
  -> rbtree: {THP-aligned PFN -> count[512]}
  -> damon_spe_folio_heatmap() -> hot bitmap
  -> split decision (hot_fraction < threshold)

  Data can be fed into the rbtree via:
  - Phase 2b: userspace SPE daemon -> debugfs spe_feed (ready)
  - Phase 2c: kernel perf_event_create_kernel_counter (requires hw)

Test Results
============

ARM64 VMware VM, kernel 7.1.0-rc5+, 4 CPUs, 4GB RAM:

  Split (PMD THP -> 16KB mTHP):
    nr_applied=11, sz_applied=70MB
    AnonHugePages: 67584kB -> 0kB
    16KB nr_anon: 0 -> 4224

  Collapse (16KB mTHP -> PMD THP):
    nr_applied=10, sz_applied=66MB
    AnonHugePages: 0kB -> 67584kB
    16KB nr_anon: 4224 -> 0

  Full round-trip verified: split then collapse, stats correct.
  No deadlocks (rwsem issue identified and fixed in patch 7).

  Benchmark (256MB anon random access, 60s, ARM64):
    DAMON madvise: +43.8% throughput vs baseline, +8.9% vs always-mode
    Full collapse completes in ~2.5s

Known Issues
============
- khugepaged can re-collapse mTHPs that DAMON splits, causing ping-pong
- SPE sampling precision vs overhead tradeoff not yet measured on
  hardware (userspace validation pending on Kunpeng 920 server)
- Without SPE hardware, split falls back to unconditional mode
  (splits all PMD THPs matching the scheme filter)

Next Steps
==========
1. Validate SPE sub-page heatmap accuracy on ARM server (Kunpeng 920)
2. Add kernel SPE event for direct sampling (Phase 2c)
3. Implement rate-limiting to prevent split/collapse ping-pong
4. Optimize SPE sampling period for production workloads

